<title>USA: Southern to shut Ala. nuke Sat. for refuel.</title>
<headline>Southern to shut Ala. nuke Sat. for refuel.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southern Nuclear Operation Co's 822 megawatt (MW) Farley nuclear unit 2 in Dothan, Ala., will shut down on Saturday, as scheduled, for maintenance and refueling, the company said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The unit will be down tomorrow. The outage should last for at least a month,&quot; company spokeswoman Loretto Stevens said.</p>
<p>Southern's other Farley unit, with a generating capacity of 812 MW, is operating at full power, she said.</p>
<p>Southern Nuclear is a unit of Southern Co.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
